{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# AI & Machine Learning: Code, Train & Deploy\n",
    "## Week 2 — Music Data Wrangling with Pandas\n",
    "\n",
    "**Syllabus focus:** Data manipulation with Pandas; loading data; filtering; grouping; aggregation; cleaning; preprocessing.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business context:** A streaming platform must clean and standardize its music data before it can evaluate fairness, popularity, and listener behavior. Dirty data silently creates bias and makes recommendations unreliable.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Capstone deliverable:** Cleaned artist and track dataset ready for analysis in Weeks 4-9.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Learning objectives\n",
    "- Load data into a pandas DataFrame\n",
    "- Inspect columns, dtypes, and missing values\n",
    "- Clean inconsistent text and invalid values\n",
    "- Create summary-level features such as popularity bands\n",
    "- Prepare a reusable dataset for later modeling\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Music industry use case\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine the platform is tracking artist and track performance across multiple regions. Some artists are mainstream and heavily represented; others are independent, niche, or new. The team needs to know how much of the catalog is actually usable for analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "This task is not only technical—it is fundamental to fair music discovery. If the dataset is messy or inconsistent, the model may incorrectly underweight underrepresented artists.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "artist_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'artist_id': ['ART-001', 'ART-002', 'ART-003', 'ART-004', 'ART-005'],\n",
    "    'artist_name': ['Nova Vela', 'Luna Harbor', 'Aster Vale', 'Bright Echo', 'Velvet Foundry'],\n",
    "    'genre': ['indie pop', 'alternative rock', 'ambient electronic', 'hip hop', 'indie pop'],\n",
    "    'monthly_listeners': [42000, 26000, 7100, 54000, 15000],\n",
    "    'total_streams': [120000, 98000, 31000, 152000, 24000],\n",
    "    'playlist_inclusion': [True, True, False, True, False],\n",
    "    'new_artist': [False, False, True, False, True],\n",
    "    'country': ['US', 'UK', 'DE', 'US', 'FR']\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(artist_df.head())\n",
    "print(f\\"Dataset rows: {len(artist_df)}\\")\n",
    "print(f\\"Columns: {list(artist_df.columns)}\\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Exercise: inspect the DataFrame\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the following checks to understand the quality of the data:\n",
    "- display column dtypes\n",
    "- identify missing values\n",
    "- detect duplicate artists\n",
    "- summarize the `genre` distribution\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(artist_df.dtypes)\n",
    "print('\\nMissing values by column:')\n",
    "print(artist_df.isnull().sum())\n",
    "print('\\nDuplicate rows:', artist_df.duplicated().sum())\n",
    "print('\\nGenre counts:')\n",
    "print(artist_df['genre'].value_counts())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cleaning and transformation\n",
    "\n",
    "Real-world data is rarely perfect. As a rule, standardize values before building models. For example, lowercase genres, ensure consistent names, and classify artists by popularity band.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "artist_df['genre_clean'] = artist_df['genre'].str.strip().str.lower()\n",
    "artist_df['popularity_band'] = pd.cut(\n",
    "    artist_df['monthly_listeners'],\n",
    "    bins=[0, 10000, 25000, 50000, float('inf')],\n",
    "    labels=['emerging', 'mid-tier', 'mainstream', 'top-tier'],\n",
    "    right=False\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(artist_df[['artist_name', 'genre_clean', 'monthly_listeners', 'popularity_band']])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Practice task: build a cleaned artist summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a summary DataFrame that shows:\n",
    "- total artists\n",
    "- average monthly listeners\n",
    "- average total streams\n",
    "- share of playlist-included artists\n",
    "- share of new artists\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'total_artists': [len(artist_df)],\n",
    "    'avg_monthly_listeners': [artist_df['monthly_listeners'].mean()],\n",
    "    'avg_total_streams': [artist_df['total_streams'].mean()],\n",
    "    'playlist_share': [artist_df['playlist_inclusion'].mean()],\n",
    "    'new_artist_share': [artist_df['new_artist'].mean()]\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(summary)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Challenge: identify long-tail artists\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the cleaned data to flag artists that appear underrepresented or emerging. For example, an artist with low monthly listeners and no playlist inclusion is likely a candidate for long-tail discovery.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "long_tail = artist_df[(artist_df['monthly_listeners'] < 20000) & (artist_df['playlist_inclusion'] == False)]\n",
    "print('Long-tail candidates:')\n",
    "print(long_tail[['artist_name', 'genre_clean', 'monthly_listeners', 'playlist_inclusion']])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Deliverable checkpoint\n",
    "This week should produce a cleaned DataFrame and summary metrics that can be used in later statistical and recommendation work.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Week 2 rubric\n",
    "- Data loaded and inspected correctly: 25%\n",
    "- Cleaning and transformation applied: 25%\n",
    "- Summary metrics interpreted correctly: 25%\n",
    "- Long-tail artist identification supported by evidence: 25%\n"
   ]
  }
